== (2) Lemma PT on FRW (sympy): S = T + f(t) g, Bianchi forces Lambda(t) - 8 pi G f(t) = const
d/dt E00 + 3H(E00+Eii) on T-conserving matter = 8*pi*G*Derivative(f(t), t) - Derivative(Lam(t), t)
=> consistency (E00=Eii=0 for all t) requires Lam' = 8 pi G f' : Lam - 8 pi G f = Lam_c, and then
   3H^2 = 8 pi G rho + Lam_c : the subtraction f(t) is invisible; only Lam_c and the true T matter.

== (3) Baum-Hawking: I_E(S^4) = -3 pi/(G Lambda) [hbar=c=1]
3 pi/(l_P^2 Lambda_obs) = 3.3087e+122  ; P(Lambda_obs/2)/P(Lambda_obs) = exp(3.309e+122)
S^4 action I(r) = pi*r**2*(Lambda*r**2 - 6)/(3*G) ; stationary r = [sqrt(3)/sqrt(Lambda)] ; I* = -3*pi/(G*Lambda) ; d2I/dr2 at r* = 8*pi/G

== (4) fixed total 4-volume V (unimodular 'microcanonical', count = V/l^4):
   Z(V) = int dLambda exp(Lambda V/(8 pi G)) exp(3 pi/(G Lambda)); saddle Lambda* = sqrt(24 pi^2 / V)
   saddle: [2*sqrt(6)*pi/sqrt(V)]
   N = V_lc (past cone) = 6.389e+242 l_P^4 -> Lambda* l_P^2 = 6.089e-121 = 21.38 Lambda_obs
   N = (c/H0)^4 = 5.200e+243 l_P^4 -> Lambda* l_P^2 = 2.134e-121 = 7.49 Lambda_obs
   N = (c t0)^4 = 4.242e+243 l_P^4 -> Lambda* l_P^2 = 2.363e-121 = 8.30 Lambda_obs
   total 4-volume giving Lambda* = Lambda_obs: 2.919e+245 l_P^4 = 56.1 (c/H0)^4 ; (Euclidean S^4 of radius sqrt(3/Lambda_obs): 8 pi^2 r^4/3 = 2.919e+245)

== (5) equilibrium (Gibbs-Duhem) identity: E(N,V)=V eps(N/V); dE/dV|_N = eps - n eps'(n) = -p
   dE/dV at fixed N = -n*Derivative(eps(n), n) + eps(n)  (= eps - n eps'(n); vanishes at the zero-pressure equilibrium)
   sample eps(n) = n(n-1)^2 - n/2: equilibrium n0 = 1.000000, eps(n0) = -0.500000, eps - n eps' = 0.00e+00
   fixed density (one record per site, fixed spacing): n = n_max is not a variable; eps(n_max) - mu n_max has no condition setting it to zero.
